NAME
    lang - resolve one technical localized message

SYNOPSIS
    lang <domain> <message-id>

DESCRIPTION
    lang resolves text from the technical sys language catalog.

    Lookup order is:
        active process-context locale, when selected
        global selected sys locale, when no context locale is selected
        en_US fallback locale
        literal <domain>.<message-id> fallback

    Catalog content is treated as UTF-8 data and is not evaluated as shell code.
    The command does not merge or resolve branded ai catalogs.

    The context locale is a process-local selection of an available direct
    locale directory. It overrides only lookup in this process and its ordinary
    children; it does not change the global language current selector. If a
    message is absent from the selected context catalog, lookup falls back to
    en_US rather than consulting the global selected locale.

OPERANDS
    <domain>
        Technical message domain.
    <message-id>
        Message identifier within the domain.

ENVIRONMENT
    Requires a nonempty m_ROOT inherited from an initialized m environment.
    An active m_CONTEXT_LOCALE selects the process-local technical catalog.
    Without that selection, lookup follows m_LANG_CURRENT_DIR.
    From an uninitialized host shell, invoke m lang [arguments].


EXIT STATUS
    0   Message resolution/output completed.
    Non-zero status indicates invalid invocation or output/runtime failure.

SEE ALSO
    lang-set
